 "changelog": [
  {
   "contract_version": 2,
   "date": "2026-09-02",
   "change": "reader_rate_range_q256 now states what the DECODER accepts, measured by encoding a unit at each candidate rate and running it through the route's own load path; the plugin refuses a declared q256 outside it (it did not before, and an allocated checkpoint carrying seven unlisted rungs served with nothing refusing). E4M3 widened from [1024,1024] to [256,2048] continuous at step 1 -- the bound is the trellis grammar's shaped domain (code rate 1..8 over an 8-bit-native alphabet), not the rungs anyone had exported. E2M1x2 stays the single point 896, bounded BELOW by the native decoder (span-2 TCQ only; the sub-cap WINDOW body has no served decode) and ABOVE by the same grammar (rate 7 of arity-2 native 8). candidate_rungs_q256 renamed attested_rungs_q256 because it never was the decodable set and reading it as one is how the gap opened: it is the rungs a lane_eligibility cell attests. Added an explicit grid to each entry so a (route, grid) pair with no published range refuses rather than resolving to another entry's numbers. candidate_rungs_q256 is retained as a DEPRECATED ALIAS of attested_rungs_q256 -- same list, refused if it disagrees -- so this stays an ADDITIVE change that a v1 reader can still read, which is why the schema string does not move. It is dropped at schema v2."
  },
  {
   "contract_version": 1,
   "date": "2026-09-01",
   "change": "First published contract: two dense families, four cells, TP1/EP0."
  }
 ]
